null},"body":"Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/6115\r\nCloses https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/5197 (somewhat; the new class has this built-in, but not Button)\r\n\r\nAdds a PopupButton class and makes MenuButton, OptionButton and ColorPickerButton inherit it. Note that it differs from the proposal, because it's supposed to provide a generic button for showing popups, so it has no methods specific for MenuButton etc. It supports switch on hover, so the 3 inheriting classes all support it now.\r\n\r\nThe button has no popup by default, you can either add one as a child node or provide it with `_create_popup()` virtual method (which is called when the popup is needed for the first time).\r\n\r\nIn a follow-up I plan to make use of the PopupButton in the editor (e.g. Control layout popups could use it).\r\n(also I forgot to add some theme items...)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114544/reactions","total_count":12,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":12,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114544/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}